      "section": "Coolant Requirements",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 47.5654,
        "t": 657.8632068359375,
        "r": 175.97499999999997,
        "b": 647.0439469606777
      },
      "content": "Coolant Requirements",
      "level": 2,
      "section_id": "sec_auto_588",
      "section_path": [
        {
          "id": "sec_8",
          "title": "8. Routine Maintenance"
        },
        {
          "id": "sec_auto_588",
          "title": "Coolant Requirements"
        }
      ],
      "parent_section_id": "sec_8",
      "section_level": 2,
      "page": 48,
      "chunk_hint": "section_heading",
      "semantic_role": "section_heading",
      "source": "pdf_text"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_0558",
      "reading_order": 589,
      "section": "Coolant Requirements",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 47.56539999999998,
        "t": 635.4885068359375,
        "r": 291.52010000000035,
        "b": 549.7170519502828
      },
      "content": "Engine coolant must inhibit corrosion and protect against freezing.  A 50/50 mixture of ethylene glycol anti-freeze and water is recommended for normal operation and storage.  Use only a reliable brand of antifreeze that contains a rust and corrosion inhibitor. The antifreeze must not contain a stop-leak additive.",
      "section_id": "sec_auto_588",
      "parent_section_id": "sec_8",
      "section_level": 2,
      "section_path": [
        {
          "id": "sec_8",
          "title": "8. Routine Maintenance"
        },
        {
          "id": "sec_auto_588",
          "title": "Coolant Requirements"
        }
      ],
      "page": 48,
      "chunk_hint": "section_start",
      "semantic_role": "overview",
      "source": "pdf_text"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_0559",
      "reading_order": 590,
      "section": "Coolant Requirements",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 47.56539999999998,
        "t": 536.9010068359377,
        "r": 291.46730000000014,
        "b": 474.11850683593747
      },
      "content": "Do not exceed a 50/50 mixture of ethylene glycol and water.  A higher proportion of ethylene glycol will alter the heat transfer properties of the coolant. A  50/50  mixture  will  provide  freeze  protection  to -34  F (-37  C).",
      "section_id": "sec_auto_588",
      "parent_section_id": "sec_8",
      "section_level": 2,
      "section_path": [
        {
          "id": "sec_8",
          "title": "8. Routine Maintenance"
        },
        {
          "id": "sec_auto_588",
          "title": "Coolant Requirements"
        }
      ],
      "page": 48,
      "chunk_hint": "continue",
      "semantic_role": "description",
      "source": "pdf_text"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_0560",
      "reading_order": 591,
      "section": "Coolant Requirements",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 47.5642,
        "t": 462.57500683593753,
        "r": 291.4759999999997,
        "b": 389.4479492035389
      },
      "content": "Water used for engine coolant should be clean, low in minerals, and free of corrosive chemicals.  Use distilled or soft water if available.  Avoid the use of well  water,  which  may  contain  minerals  that  can clog the heat exchanger core and reduce cooling efficiency.",
      "section_id": "sec_auto_588",
      "parent_section_id": "sec_8",
      "section_level": 2,
      "section_path": [
        {
          "id": "sec_8",
          "title": "8. Routine Maintenance"
        },
        {
          "id": "sec_auto_588",
          "title": "Coolant Requirements"
        }
      ],
      "page": 48,
      "chunk_hint": "continue",
      "semantic_role": "description",
      "source": "pdf_text"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "id": "txt_0561",
      "reading_order": 592,
      "section": "Filling the Cooling System",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 47.5654,
        "t": 376.60970683593746,
        "r": 198.7882,
        "b": 365.79044696067757
      },
      "content": "Filling the Cooling System",
      "level": 2,
      "section_id": "sec_auto_592",
      "section_path": [
        {
          "id": "sec_8",
          "title": "8. Routine Maintenance"
        },
        {
          "id": "sec_auto_592",
          "title": "Filling the Cooling System"
        }
      ],
      "parent_section_id": "sec_8",
      "section_level": 2,
      "page": 48,
      "chunk_hint": "section_heading",
      "semantic_role": "section_heading",
      "source": "pdf_text"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_0562",
      "reading_order": 593,
      "section": "Filling the Cooling System",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 47.5654,
        "t": 354.2350068359375,
        "r": 291.47499999999985,
        "b": 306.3925492035388
      },
      "content": "Verify that all drain cocks are closed and all hose clamps are secure.  Remove the cooling system pressure cap and slowly fill the cooling system with the coolant mixture.",
      "section_id": "sec_auto_592",
      "parent_section_id": "sec_8",
      "section_level": 2,
      "section_path": [
        {
          "id": "sec_8",
          "title": "8. Routine Maintenance"
        },
        {
          "id": "sec_auto_592",
          "title": "Filling the Cooling System"
        }
      ],
      "page": 48,
      "chunk_hint": "section_start",
      "semantic_role": "overview",
      "source": "pdf_text"
    },
    {
      "type": "admonition",
      "id": "txt_0563",
      "reading_order": 594,
      "section": "Filling the Cooling System",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 47.565599999999996,
        "t": 292.4397068359375,
        "r": 291.44330000000014,
        "b": 231.9528519502826
      },
      "content": "CAUTION Exceeding  the  recommended  fill rate can cause incomplete filling of the engine block, leading to engine damage during warmup.  Always follow the recommended fill procedure.",
      "severity": "caution",
      "section_id": "sec_auto_592",
      "parent_section_id": "sec_8",
      "section_level": 2,
      "section_path": [
        {
          "id": "sec_8",
          "title": "8. Routine Maintenance"
        },
        {
          "id": "sec_auto_592",
          "title": "Filling the Cooling System"
        }
      ],
      "page": 48,
      "chunk_hint": "admonition",
      "semantic_role": "caution",
      "source": "pdf_text"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_0564",
      "reading_order": 595,
      "section": "Filling the Cooling System",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 320.93870000000004,
        "t": 737.9903068359375,
        "r": 564.7536999999998,
        "b": 715.4324492035388
      },
      "content": "Add coolant to the recovery tank (or separate expansion tank if equipped) to the full-cold level.",
      "section_id": "sec_auto_592",
      "parent_section_id": "sec_8",
      "section_level": 2,
      "section_path": [
        {
          "id": "sec_8",
          "title": "8. Routine Maintenance"
        },
        {
          "id": "sec_auto_592",
          "title": "Filling the Cooling System"
        }
      ],
      "page": 48,
      "chunk_hint": "continue",
      "semantic_role": "description",
      "source": "pdf_text"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_0565",
      "reading_order": 596,
      "section": "Filling the Cooling System",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 320.93870000000004,
        "t": 687.5344068359376,
        "r": 565.0111000000002,
        "b": 626.992449203539
      },
      "content": "Start the engine, then remove the pressure cap and monitor the coolant level.  As trapped air is expelled from the system, the coolant level will drop.  Add coolant  to  replace  it.    Replace  the  pressure  cap when the coolant level is stable.",
      "section_id": "sec_auto_592",
      "parent_section_id": "sec_8",
      "section_level": 2,
      "section_path": [
        {
          "id": "sec_8",
          "title": "8. Routine Maintenance"
        },
        {
          "id": "sec_auto_592",
          "title": "Filling the Cooling System"
        }
      ],
      "page": 48,
